{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Now I know that you are a God-fearer.</b> Not every expression of ״עַתָּה״ ('now') limits the time before it — for we find (Deuteronomy 10:12) ״וְעַתָּה יִשְׂרָאֵל מָה ה׳ שׁוֹאֵל מֵעִמָּךְ כִּי אִם לְיִרְאָה״ — 'And now, Israel, what does HaShem ask of you but to fear?' Was it only before this that He did not ask fear of him? Rather, it is as though He said, 'Behold, Israel.' So too, ״עַתָּה יָדַעְתִּי״ is as though He said, 'Behold, I have known.'" "And there are those who say: ״יָדַעְתִּי״ ('I have known') is like ״הוֹדַעְתִּי״ ('I have made known'), for the purpose of this trial was in order to raise a banner, a standard, to show the nations the beauty of his deeds. And the statement ״וְהָאֱלֹהִים נִסָּה״ ('and Elohim tested') is an expression of the raising of a standard, visible to every person — for open rebuke that comes from hidden love is better (Proverbs 27:5): when the love is great but hidden, the Holy One, blessed be He, sends upon him open rebuke, and through his accepting it out of love, his love will be revealed and shown before the eyes of all.\n\nNow, regarding the matter of HaShem's knowledge of every thing before it comes into being, and that man nonetheless remains upon his free choice — many have become entangled in this inquiry, and most of those who investigate it went out to glean and found no sufficient way to resolve this doubt, for the two appear to contradict one another, and it is a deep matter — who can find it? And upon this did the Rambam, of blessed memory, explain their saying (Avot 3:15) ״הַכֹּל צָפוּי וְהָרְשׁוּת נְתוּנָה״ ('All is foreseen, yet permission is given'): for even though all is foreseen before Him, blessed be He, nonetheless permission is given to man, and he remains upon his free choice."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:29:11.412222107Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}